  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d95f71226bf26bc4caed6a0458a3b538, type: 3}
  m_Name: Lesson 25 Question 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: What does the Bible say about our good works?
  answers:
  - They are perfect
  - They are polluted by sin
  - God accepts them
  - Everyone can do good works
  correctAnswerIndex: 1
  discussionAnswer: The Bible says no one does good works on their own because everyone's
    works are corrupted by sin. Only Jesus' good works are perfect. God counts Jesus'
    works to our account when we believe in Him.
